    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0168" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5241c</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-08T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 8, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4958. Ask British authorities to ascertain if Reuter or any other news
                    organization has forwarded presidential communication to Russia to any other
                    country or agency, to be held for release. If so, have Reuter or other agency
                    recall all copies. The message is in the hands of Reuter through an error here.
                    The communication will not be published until certain important alterations are
                    made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
